{
  "q1_accurate": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "consul.Server", "note": "retained_via_interfaces gave all 31 interface-typed holders with file:line, via-interface, carrier and chain — the entire Step 4/5 audit (raftHandle->raft.Backend, PeeringBackend->peerstream/peering, caDelegateWithState->CAManager/ca.ConsulProvider, v1ServiceExportsShim->multicluster controllers) came straight from these rows and I cited them verbatim"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "consul.Server", "note": "composed_by listed every direct *Server-field endpoint (ACL, Catalog, Health, KVS, Session, Txn, etc.) with exact struct file:line used for Group A; includes gave the two embedding wrappers serverACLResolverBackend and caDelegateWithState"},
    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "cluster server that the agent runs, main server struct handling RPCs and Raft", "note": "top hits pointed at agent/consul/server.go and rpc.go, correctly identifying the rework target consul.Server @ server.go:169"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "setupGRPCServices", "note": "callees resolved the wiring hub location server_grpc.go:181 and each per-service registrar (registerPeeringServer:409, registerConnectCAServer:477, etc.) with call-site lines used for Step 3 trace"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "consul.Server.Shutdown", "note": "gave the Shutdown ref server.go:1241 that I then read for the teardown-signal contract"}
  ],
  "q1_wrong": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "consul.Server", "note": "carrier attribution is a heuristic: rows for connectca/serverdiscovery EventPublisher and OverviewManager/usagemetrics StateProvider were labeled with carrier PeeringBackend/caDelegateWithState but actually hold s.publisher/s.fsm at runtime — I had to read server_grpc.go and NewServer to reclassify them as state-not-server (the tool disclosed this in retained_note, so it flagged its own uncertainty)"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "consul.Server.Shutdown", "note": "callees returned only 1 resolved edge with 11 low-confidence hidden; not wrong but near-empty, so I read the function body directly instead"}
  ],
  "q2_fallbacks": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "consul.Server", "fallback": "read", "missing": "rows give the holder/field location but not which concrete satisfier is assigned at runtime, so I read server_grpc.go:409-530 and NewServer to confirm FSMServer=s, Backend=PeeringBackend, and to separate the genuine-server holders from state-holders"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "consul.Server.Shutdown", "fallback": "read", "missing": "method body / teardown steps — graph gives edges not the sequence of close(shutdownCh) and component shutdowns I needed for Step 2"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "consul.Server (composed_by)", "fallback": "read", "missing": "field type/name detail — I read acl_server.go, leader_connect_ca.go, peering_backend.go, raft_handle.go, configentry/server.go to confirm embed-vs-pointer and the Config-embedding pattern"}
  ],
  "q3_hints": [
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query_before": "consul.Server callers depth 1", "query_after": "consul.Server blast max_hops 4", "hint": "next_steps: '54 callers reach this - run sense_blast for full change impact and what holds it (retained_via_interfaces...)' — this pushed me to run the blast that produced the entire interface-holder audit"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query_before": "setupGRPCServices (unknown location)", "query_after": "sense_graph symbol setupGRPCServices", "hint": "CLAUDE.md 'grepping a name -> Sense' plus sense_search not surfacing it directly led me to resolve its ref via sense_graph rather than grep"}
  ],
  "q4_value": "The retained_via_interfaces rows in a single sense_blast call — they surfaced the entire class of holders whose field is a locally-declared interface that never names or imports consul.Server (raftHandle->raft.Backend, v1ServiceExportsShim->multicluster controllers), which is exactly the easy-to-miss set the ticket demanded and which grep-for-Server would never have found.",
  "q5_improve": "Let a blast row optionally report the runtime assignment site (where the interface field is set in the constructor/wiring) so I don't have to read server_grpc.go to distinguish 'holds the server' from 'holds s.publisher/s.fsm' — the carrier heuristic's own false positives would collapse.",
  "score": 9,
  "score_rationale": "The retained_via_interfaces set (Q1) delivered transitive, interface-hidden holders across five packages that no grep for the Server type could recover, and the only fallbacks (Q2) were reading bodies for behavior/runtime-assignment detail Sense never claims to give — a genuine capability beyond grep/read within this session."
}

